    "logic": {
      "concept": "A trend resumes from a structural pivot, not from an arbitrary bar. A Semafor swing over 8 bars marks the pivot, RSI(14) leaving an extreme says momentum re-engaged after it, and a close crossing EMA(9) is the bar to act on; the smoothed Heiken Ashi ribbon over EMA(20)/EMA(5) refuses the setups that form against the macro lean. The pivot is CONFIRMED 8 bars after it forms, never read centred, so no signal depends on a bar that had not printed. Trades are attributed by their ENTRY bar, never the exit, so a move opened in one quadrant that runs into another still scores where it opened.",
      "entry": "LONG when Close crosses ABOVE EMA(9), a swing LOW was confirmed within the last 5 bars, and RSI(14) crossed above 30.0 at or after that pivot. SHORT when Close crosses BELOW EMA(9), a swing HIGH was confirmed within 5 bars, and RSI crossed below 70.0 at or after it. With use_macro_trend the long side additionally needs the smoothed Heiken Ashi candle green and rising under the close, and the short side its mirror.",
      "exit": "The opposite trigger always closes the position. With use_midline_exit=True a close crossing back through EMA(9) closes it too, and with use_rsi_zone_exit=False so does RSI entering the opposite extreme - 70.0 for a long, 30.0 for a short. A protective stop at 1.5 x ATR(14) sits underneath all of them, trailing=False. No ATR take-profit is modelled (tp_atr_mult=None): the RSI zone is the target and it is a SIGNAL, because the engine has no target orders."
    }
  },
